{"name":"Angel Touch","hex":"#dddfd8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incorporeal and holy or semidivine messenger from a deity or other divine entity, traditionally depicted as a youthful, winged figure in flowing robes.\n\n One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues.","One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To support by donating money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel"},{"term":"touch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Primarily physical senses.\n To make physical contact with; to bring the hand, finger or other part of the body into contact with. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To make physical contact with; to bring the hand, finger or other part of the body into contact with. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of touching, especially with the hand or finger.","The faculty or sense of perception by physical contact."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel"},{"title":"Somatosensory system","blocks":[{"text":"The somatosensory system, or somatic 